note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note omegese-om2.md 2 lines 53-55: 0x then 1..16 digits 0-9a-f, value unsigned, typed by the place
note under the decimal range rule. Maxima of every integer type, 0x0, 16 digits with leading zeros,
note and all sixteen digits. Expected stdout: oracle/s0s2/oracle.py (hex_max). Used with lib/putu.om.
om2
fn main to int
a = uchar 0xff
putu ulong a
b = ushort 0xffff
putu ulong b
c = uint 0xffffffff
putu ulong c
d = ulong 0xffffffffffffffff
putu d
e = byte 0x7f
putu ulong e
f = short 0x7fff
putu ulong f
g = int 0x7fffffff
putu ulong g
h = long 0x7fffffffffffffff
putu ulong h
z = ulong 0x0
putu z
y = uchar 0x00000000000000ff
putu ulong y
w = ulong 0x0123456789abcdef
putu w
ret 0
end
